# Cross-link keep-out list. Documents/surveys deliberately NOT in any corpus group.
# `crosslink.py coverage` reports every survey/wiki that is neither grouped
# (.claude/crosslink-scope) nor listed here, so a new document is never silently
# unscanned.
#
# One path per line: a file, or a directory (all its top-level chapters kept out).
# `#` comments allowed. Adding an entry here is a DELIBERATE "do not cross-link this".
#
# The mirror image of a corpus group: a group says "link these together", this file
# says "these belong to no group, on purpose". A survey that is neither is a bug.

# --- Tooling fixture, not research content ---------------------------------
# The worked reference example that every gate step is validated against. It is
# deliberately self-contained: cross-links into the real corpus would couple the
# fixture to content that changes, which is exactly what a fixture must not do.
surveys/attention-demo
